(version 1)
# 4-layer fab rules, 5/5 mil variant (CR, operator ruling 2026-11-11). Identical to
# fab_4layer_oshpark_pcbway.kicad_dru except track width and copper clearance, which take the 5 mil
# (0.127 mm) values that both fabs offer: [OSH] 4-layer 5 mil trace / 5 mil space; [PCBP] 5/5 mil option.
# Operator statement 2026-11-11: PCBWay standard service is 6/6 mil on 1 oz and 2 oz copper; 5/5 mil only with
# 1 oz copper. A CR ordered with this rule file therefore uses 1 oz outer copper (A.8 Copper fallback).
# 4-layer fab rules (CR). Each value is the MORE CONSERVATIVE of OSH Park standard 4-layer and
# PCBWay standard PCB, read from the fabs' pages on 2026-11-10:
#   [OSH]  https://docs.oshpark.com/services/four-layer/
#   [PCBW] https://www.pcbway.com/capabilities.html  (standard section covers 1-14 layers; "Advanced PCB" table where noted)
#   [PCBP] https://www.pcbway.com/pcb_prototype/      (order-form options)
# To use: copy this file next to the project as <project>.kicad_dru. Mask expansion, mask web and
# board thickness are board-setup values, not custom-rule constraints: apply them with
# apply_board_setup.py.
# Note: the [OSH] 4-layer changelog (28-JAN-2026) mentions a "temporary alternate stackup" for some
# orders; its details are in images that were not read. TODO(verify: OSH Park) the stackup.

# Trace width. [OSH] 5 mil (0.127 mm). [PCBW] standard 4 mil (0.1 mm); Advanced table, 1 oz outer,
# normal process ">=5/6 mil" (width/spacing). [PCBP] offers 4/4, 5/5, 6/6 mil.
# More conservative = 5 mil; set to 6 mil so the PCBWay order can use the 6/6 option.
# TODO(verify): which PCBWay track/space option is the base price (page does not say).
(rule "fab_track_width"
  (constraint track_width (min 0.127mm)))

# Copper-to-copper clearance. [OSH] 5 mil (0.127 mm). [PCBW] standard "Min Spacing" 4 mil (0.1 mm);
# Advanced 1 oz outer normal process 6 mil. Rule: 6 mil.
(rule "fab_clearance"
  (constraint clearance (min 0.127mm)))

# Copper-to-board-edge. [OSH] 15 mil (0.381 mm) "from nominal board edge". [PCBW] Advanced, CNC
# milling, normal process 0.25 mm. Rule: 0.381 mm.
(rule "fab_edge_clearance"
  (constraint edge_clearance (min 0.381mm)))

# Minimum drill, PTH and via. [OSH] "Minimum Drill Size" 10 mil (0.254 mm); drilled vs finished not
# stated. [PCBW] 0.15 mm minimum, but "Any holes ... smaller than 0.2mm will be subject to extra
# charges"; Advanced: 0.2 mm hole allowed up to 1.6 mm board. Rule: 0.254 mm.
# TODO(verify: OSH Park) whether 10 mil is drilled or finished; a 0.3 mm via drill clears both readings.
(rule "fab_hole_size"
  (constraint hole_size (min 0.254mm)))

# Annular ring. [OSH] 4 mil (0.1016 mm). [PCBW] "Min Width of Annular Ring" 0.15 mm (6 mil).
# Rule: 0.15 mm.
(rule "fab_annular_ring"
  (constraint annular_width (min 0.15mm)))

# Via pad diameter. Neither fab states a value. Derived: min drill 0.254 + 2 x 0.15 ring = 0.554 mm.
(rule "fab_via_diameter"
  (condition "A.Type == 'Via'")
  (constraint via_diameter (min 0.554mm)))

# Hole-to-hole (edge to edge). [OSH] no minimum; 5 mil (0.127 mm) recommended. [PCBW] Advanced,
# normal process: component hole 16 mil (0.4064 mm); via <= 0.45 mm: 11 mil (0.2794 mm).
# Rule: 0.4064 mm in general, 0.2794 mm between two vias. TODO(verify: PCBWay) that the Advanced
# figures are edge-to-edge (the page does not define the measure).
(rule "fab_hole_to_hole"
  (constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.4064mm)))
(rule "fab_hole_to_hole_via_via"
  (condition "A.Type == 'Via' && B.Type == 'Via'")
  (constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.2794mm)))

# Plated hole to inner-layer copper. [OSH] "plated drill to internal copper clearance" 10 mil
# (0.254 mm). [PCBW] not found in the standard section. Rule: 0.254 mm on inner layers.
(rule "fab_hole_to_inner_copper"
  (layer inner)
  (constraint hole_clearance (min 0.254mm)))

# Silkscreen text. [OSH] line 5 mil (0.127 mm) recommended, 3 mil for short lines/text; text height
# not stated. [PCBW] character width 0.15 mm, height 0.8 mm, width:height 1:5.
# Rule: height >= 0.8 mm, stroke >= 0.15 mm (keep stroke >= height/5 for taller text).
# Silkscreen line width has no custom-rule constraint: draw silk lines at >= 0.15 mm.
(rule "fab_silk_text"
  (layer "?.Silkscreen")
  (constraint text_height (min 0.8mm))
  (constraint text_thickness (min 0.15mm)))

# Not expressible as constraints (see apply_board_setup.py):
#   Solder-mask expansion: [OSH] value not stated; "Maximum soldermask alignment" 3 mil "Covers
#     retraction, expansion, and shift". [PCBW] Advanced "solder mask opening" >= 2 mil normal.
#     Setting: 0.0508 mm (2 mil). TODO(verify) against both fabs' preferred expansion.
#   Solder-mask web: [OSH] 4 mil (0.1016 mm). [PCBW] green, < 2 oz: 4 mil (>= 4.5 mil black).
#     Setting: 0.1016 mm (use green mask at PCBWay; other colours need 0.1143 mm).
#   Board thickness: [OSH] 63 mil (1.6 mm) nominal. [PCBP] "1.6mm (Default)". Setting: 1.6 mm.
#   Copper weight: [OSH] outer 1 oz, inner 1/2 oz. [PCBW] outer 1-8 oz, inner 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 4 oz
#     (no 1/2 oz); defaults not stated. Design current paths for the thinner value: 1 oz outer,
#     0.5 oz inner. TODO(verify: PCBWay) that 1 oz outer / 1 oz inner is the base price.
#   Free mask colours at PCBWay: green, red, yellow, blue. Free silk colours: white, black.
